=== HTML ===
<style>
	/* Some properties flow down to children automatically */
	body {
		font-family: sans-serif;
		color: #333;
	}

	/* Others do not ~ this border stays on the div */
	.card {
		border: 2px solid #ccc;
		padding: 12px;
	}

	/* Specificity: which rule wins when two of them apply */
	p {
		color: navy;
	}
	.note {
		color: green;
	}
	#special {
		color: crimson;
	}

	/* Later rule wins when specificity ties */
	.late {
		color: orange;
	}
	.late {
		color: purple;
	}
</style>

<div class="card">
	<p>I inherited the font and colour from &lt;body&gt;, but not the border.</p>
</div>

<p>Just a p ~ navy.</p>
<p class="note">p and .note ~ the class wins, so green.</p>
<p class="note" id="special">p, .note and #special ~ the id wins, so crimson.</p>
<p class="late">Two identical selectors ~ the last one wins, so purple.</p>
